# Prefabs & Configuration Rules

## Prefabs
- Any game object created dynamically (collectables, effects, projectiles) MUST be a Prefab in Cocos Creator.
- Procedural node creation (`new Node()`, `addComponent()` inside code) is FORBIDDEN for designer-configured objects.
- Prefabs are passed via `@property(Prefab)` and instantiated via `instantiate(prefab)` ONLY during `BootState` (pool prewarm).
- FORBIDDEN to call `instantiate()` during active `GameplayState`.

## LevelConfig — Single Source of Truth
- All numeric game constants (speeds, scales, thresholds, timers) that a designer might want to change MUST live in `LevelConfig.ts`.
- FORBIDDEN to hardcode game parameters inside components.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
this._speed = LEVEL_CONFIG.holeDefaultSpeed;

// ❌ WRONG
this._speed = 6; // magic number in component
```
